    <string name="settings_try_reset_island">Try the reset island</string>
    <string name="reset_island_demo_message">Claude weekly limit reset</string>
    <string name="reset_island_service_label">Headroom reset island</string>
    <string name="reset_island_service_description">Draws the reset island, a small pill above the camera cutout that shows when one of your limits has reset. It does not read anything on your screen, and it does not read other apps.</string>
    <string name="island_setup_title">Turn on the reset island</string>
    <string name="island_setup_intro">When a limit resets while Headroom is in the background, a small black pill grows out of your camera cutout. It shows the provider and which limit reset, waits a few seconds, and shrinks back.</string>
    <string name="island_setup_why_title">Why it needs accessibility access</string>
    <string name="island_setup_why_body">Android lets only an accessibility service draw above the status bar and on the lock screen. Headroom uses one for this and nothing else.</string>
    <string name="island_setup_not_title">What it does not do</string>
    <string name="island_setup_not_body">It does not read your screen. It does not read other apps. It asks Android for no accessibility events at all.</string>
    <string name="island_setup_turn_on_title">Turn on the service</string>
    <string name="island_setup_turn_on_body">Open accessibility settings, find Headroom reset island, turn it on, and confirm. Then come back here.</string>
    <string name="island_setup_turn_on_body_restricted">Open accessibility settings, find Headroom reset island, and try to turn it on. Android may say that it is a restricted setting. If it does, do step 2.</string>
    <string name="island_setup_turn_on_button">Open accessibility settings</string>
    <string name="island_setup_restricted_title">If Android blocks it</string>
    <string name="island_setup_restricted_body">Android blocks accessibility access for apps installed from an APK file. Open Headroom\'s App info, tap the three dots at the top right, and choose Allow restricted settings. Then do step 1 again.</string>
    <string name="island_setup_restricted_button">Open App info</string>
    <string name="island_setup_connecting">Almost there. Android is starting the service.</string>
    <string name="island_setup_done_title">The reset island is ready</string>
    <string name="island_setup_done_body">It will show up when a limit resets and Headroom is in the background. You can turn the service off in accessibility settings at any time.</string>
    <string name="island_setup_try">Try it</string>
    <string name="island_setup_close">Done</string>
